    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Stanford Global Currents is an NEH-funded Project in allegiance with McGill University and ETS in Montreal, and Groningen University in the Netherlands. Stanford's specific project focuses on British manuscripts from the long twelfth century in the Parker on the Web repository to determine how manuscript producers assisted audiences in finding their way around the folio. The Stanford Global Currents project website (link below) contains information about our work and our anticipated results. Preliminary findings are available in 'Discovery' and 'Research', where we show the components of a manuscript's mise-en-page that are being investigated by the team.\r\n\r\nThe Stanford Team is led by Professor Elaine Treharne, with investigators Professor Mark Algee-Hewitt and Dr Benjamin Albritton. Celena Allen manages the project and its undergraduate Research Assistants in the collaborative Center for Spatial and Textual Analysis, directed by Professor Zephyr Frank. The overall PI for the multi-institutional 'Global Currents: Literary Networks, c. 1090-1900' team is Professor Andrew Piper at McGill University. He has brought together teams working on Chinese books, European journals, and British manuscripts to determine how various computer programs can assist scholars interested in specific facets of book production through the centuries. Early results are very promising.\r\n\r\nIn the second year of the grant, Stanford RAs isolated features of mise-en-page for Professor Mohamed Cheriet's lab at ETS in Montreal to analyze. The final results of the image analysis done by Mohamed Cheriet's team are available here, divided into sets according to the features that were being detected: litterae notabiliores, enlarged capitals, rubrics, and intertextual space.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Treharne, Elaine and Albritton, Benjamin and Allen, Celena and Algee-Hewitt, Mark and Arabnejad, Ehsan and Cheriet, Mohamed. (2015-2016). Stanford Global Currents: Datasets from Feature Recognition Analysis. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at: https://purl.stanford.edu/mx001kp8378",
            "type": "preferred citation",
            "identifier": [],
            "displayLabel": "Preferred Citation",
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
